        "filename": "Edinburgh from Salisbury Crags Radical Road.jpg",
        "caption": "Panoramic view over Holyrood Park from the Radical Road track between the Salisbury Crags cliffs and the large and steep talus slope down to the park roads: this track was given its name after it was surfaced in the aftermath of the Radical War of 1820, using the labour of unemployed weavers from the west of Scotland at the suggestion of Walter Scott.",
